#: ../../../how-to/install-pipx.rst:3
msgid "Install pipx"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/install-pipx.rst:5
msgid "Get pipx onto your system and add its app directory to your ``PATH``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/install-pipx.rst:7
msgid "pipx runs on macOS, Linux, and Windows."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/install-pipx.rst:9
msgid "Packaging status"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/install-pipx.rst:15
msgid "Check the requirements"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/install-pipx.rst:17
msgid ""
"Installing pipx needs Python 3.10 or newer; the apps it runs can target "
"Python 3.3 or newer. Without Python 3.10, see the `Python 3 installation "
"guide <https://realpython.com/installing-python/>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/install-pipx.rst:20
msgid ""
"You also need ``pip`` for ``python3``. The steps vary by system; see `pip's "
"installation instructions <https://pip.pypa.io/en/stable/installation/>`_. "
"On Linux, install through a `Linux package manager <https://packaging.python."
"org/guides/installing-using-linux-tools/#installing-pip-setuptools-wheel-"
"with-linux-package-managers>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/install-pipx.rst:26
msgid "Install per OS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/install-pipx.rst:29
msgid "macOS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/install-pipx.rst:31
msgid ""
"$ brew install pipx\n"
"$ pipx ensurepath"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/install-pipx.rst:37
msgid "Linux"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/install-pipx.rst:39
msgid "Ubuntu 23.04 or newer:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/install-pipx.rst:41
msgid ""
"$ sudo apt update\n"
"$ sudo apt install pipx\n"
"$ pipx ensurepath"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/install-pipx.rst:47
msgid "Fedora:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/install-pipx.rst:49
msgid ""
"$ sudo dnf install pipx\n"
"$ pipx ensurepath"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/install-pipx.rst:54
msgid "Other distributions, using ``pip``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/install-pipx.rst:56
msgid ""
"$ python3 -m pip install --user pipx\n"
"$ python3 -m pipx ensurepath"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/install-pipx.rst:63
msgid ""
"Distributions that adopt `PEP 668 <https://peps.python.org/pep-0668/>`_ "
"(Ubuntu 23.04+, Debian 12+, Fedora 38+) mark the system Python as externally "
"managed, so ``pip install --user`` fails with ``externally-managed-"
"environment``. Use the distribution package (``apt install pipx``, ``dnf "
"install pipx``). If none exists, install pipx into its own virtual "
"environment:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/install-pipx.rst:68
msgid ""
"$ python3 -m venv ~/.local/share/pipx-venv\n"
"$ ~/.local/share/pipx-venv/bin/pip install pipx\n"
"$ ln -s ~/.local/share/pipx-venv/bin/pipx ~/.local/bin/pipx\n"
"$ pipx ensurepath"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/install-pipx.rst:76
msgid "Windows"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/install-pipx.rst:78
msgid "Install via `Scoop <https://scoop.sh/>`_:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/install-pipx.rst:80
msgid ""
"$ scoop install pipx\n"
"$ pipx ensurepath"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/install-pipx.rst:85
msgid ""
"Install via pip (needs pip 19.0 or newer; replace ``py`` with ``python3`` if "
"you installed Python from the Microsoft Store):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/install-pipx.rst:88
msgid "$ py -m pip install --user pipx"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/install-pipx.rst:92
msgid ""
"This often ends with a warning that ``pipx.exe`` is installed in a directory "
"that is not on ``PATH``. Go to that directory and run the executable "
"directly to fix it (run this even without the warning):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/install-pipx.rst:95
msgid "$ .\\pipx.exe ensurepath"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/install-pipx.rst:99
msgid ""
"This adds both that directory and ``%USERPROFILE%\\.local\\bin`` to your "
"search path. Restart the terminal, then confirm ``pipx`` runs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/install-pipx.rst:103
msgid "FreeBSD"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/install-pipx.rst:105
msgid ""
"$ pkg install -y py311-pipx\n"
"$ pipx ensurepath"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/install-pipx.rst:110
msgid "Or via pip:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/install-pipx.rst:112
msgid ""
"$ pip install --user pipx\n"
"$ pipx ensurepath"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/install-pipx.rst:119
msgid "Optional PATH commands"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/install-pipx.rst:121
msgid "Add the global app directory to the system ``PATH`` (pipx 1.5.0+):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/install-pipx.rst:123
msgid "$ sudo pipx ensurepath --global"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/install-pipx.rst:127
msgid ""
"Prepend the pipx bin directory instead of appending it, so pipx apps win "
"over system apps of the same name (pipx 1.7.0+):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/install-pipx.rst:130
msgid "$ sudo pipx ensurepath --prepend"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/install-pipx.rst:134
msgid ""
"For where these directories live and how to change them, see :doc:`configure-"
"paths`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/install-pipx.rst:138
msgid ""
"Some distributions ship older pipx versions (Ubuntu 24.04 ships 1.4.3). If "
"``--global`` or ``--prepend`` fails with \"unrecognized arguments\", :doc:"
"`upgrade pipx <upgrade-pipx>` first."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/install-pipx.rst:143
msgid ""
"``sudo pipx`` reports \"command not found\" when pipx lives in your user "
"directory. See :ref:`sudo-pipx-not-found` for the fix."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/install-pipx.rst:148
msgid "Run pipx without installing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/install-pipx.rst:150
msgid ""
"Download the zipapp from `GitHub releases <https://github.com/pypa/pipx/"
"releases>`_ and invoke it with a Python 3.10+ interpreter:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/install-pipx.rst:153
msgid "$ python pipx.pyz ensurepath"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/install-pipx.rst:159
msgid "Self-managed pipx"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/install-pipx.rst:161
msgid ""
"Let pipx manage its own installation so ``pipx upgrade pipx`` keeps it "
"current and you avoid distro packages that ship older versions. Bootstrap it "
"through a throwaway virtual environment:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/install-pipx.rst:164
msgid ""
"$ python3 -m venv /tmp/bootstrap\n"
"$ /tmp/bootstrap/bin/pip install pipx\n"
"$ /tmp/bootstrap/bin/pipx install pipx\n"
"$ /tmp/bootstrap/bin/pipx ensurepath\n"
"$ rm -rf /tmp/bootstrap"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/install-pipx.rst:172
msgid ""
"After this, ``pipx upgrade pipx`` upgrades pipx like any other managed app. "
"On Windows, pipx cannot delete its own running executable, so it moves "
"locked files to a trash directory and cleans them up on the next run."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/install-pipx.rst:179
msgid "Install from source control"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/install-pipx.rst:181
msgid ""
"pipx accepts any source pip supports, including git repositories. Using "
"``black`` as an example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/install-pipx.rst:183
msgid ""
"$ pipx install git+https://github.com/psf/black.git\n"
"$ pipx install git+ssh://git@github.com/psf/black\n"
"$ pipx install git+https://github.com/psf/black.git@branch\n"
"$ pipx install git+https://github.com/psf/black."
"git@ce14fa8b497bae2b50ec48b3bd7022573a59cdb1\n"
"$ pipx install https://github.com/psf/black/archive/18.9b0.zip"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/install-pipx.rst:191
msgid "Use a direct URL requirement to install extras:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/install-pipx.rst:193
msgid ""
"$ pipx install \"black[jupyter] @ git+https://github.com/psf/black.git\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/install-pipx.rst:197
msgid ""
"To test a package from an open pull request, find the fork owner and branch "
"on the PR page, then build the git URL. For PR #794 from user "
"``contributor`` on branch ``fix-something``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/install-pipx.rst:200
msgid ""
"$ pipx install git+https://github.com/contributor/pipx.git@fix-something"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/install-pipx.rst:204
msgid "If the branch is already merged, use the merge commit hash instead:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/install-pipx.rst:206
msgid "$ pipx install git+https://github.com/pypa/pipx.git@abc123def"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/install-pipx.rst:212
msgid "Verify it"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/install-pipx.rst:214
msgid "$ pipx --version"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/install-pipx.rst:218
msgid ""
"Open a new terminal after ``pipx ensurepath`` so the updated ``PATH`` takes "
"effect, then run ``pipx list`` to confirm the environment is reachable."
msgstr ""
